 "note": "Verifier unanimity = all verifier labels identical (under ANLI's protocol a 3rd verifier is added only when the first 2 disagree, so this equals 'the first two agreed'). model_label is the label ANLI's model-in-the-loop predicted for the example; the 'x' bucket holds rows whose model_label is missing or unrecognised. match/differ/no_majority partition each (gold, model_label) cell by whether the writer's gold equals / differs from / lacks a strict verifier majority. P1 (structural) bets model_label != gold on >95% of rows with a recognised model_label (the adversarial-filter construction, a finding either way). P2 (directional) bets the verifier unanimous rate spans >0.03 across model_label buckets in at least one gold class. P3 (structural) bets the gold==verifier-majority rate exceeds 0.95 in every (gold, model_label) cell with >=100 examples. per_gold_aggregate reproduces audit 45's per-class table. This audit measures AGREEMENT, not label correctness."
}